      <memberdef kind="variable" id="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_tex_cache_1ad01183dba750034a7075dea760f9affe" prot="public" static="yes" constexpr="yes" mutable="no">
        <type>std::size_t</type>
        <definition>std::size_t AGRemapCore::TexCache::DefaultMaxBytes</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>DefaultMaxBytes</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::TexCache::DefaultMaxBytes</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= 256u * 1024u * 1024u</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
How many bytes of decoded pixels to keep before evicting the least recently used
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

Decoded pixels are RGBA8 and so far larger than the file they came from -- a
4096x4096 texture is 64MB decoded. This is a budget rather than an entry count for
that reason: a handful of big textures must not be allowed to hold half a gigabyte
on the 16GB laptop this library is also developed on
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
